{"name":"Sweet Serenade","hex":"#ffc5d5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"serenade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A love song that is sung directly to one's love interest, especially one performed below the window of a loved one in the evening.","An instrumental composition in several movements."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sing or play a serenade for (someone).","To woo someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serenade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Serenade","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweet Serenade\" is a song by American hip hop recording artist Pusha T from his debut studio album My Name Is My Name (2013). \"Sweet Serenade\" features vocals from American singer Chris Brown, with production by Swizz Beatz and Kanye West. On September 4, 2013, the song was released to iTunes as the album's third official single by GOOD Music and Def Jam Recordings. The song peaked at number 19 on the US Billboard Bubbling Under Hot 100 Singles chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Serenade"},{"title":"Serenade","blocks":[{"text":"In music, a serenade is a musical composition or performance delivered in honour of someone or something. Serenades are typically calm, light pieces of music. The term comes from the Italian word serenata, which itself derives from the Latin serenus. The sense was influenced by Italian sera \"evening\", from Latin sera, fem. of serus \"late\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg/330px-Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serenade"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/df/Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg/250px-Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/df/Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg/250px-Sweet-serenade-pusha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweet-serenade-pusha.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg/500px-Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg/500px-Judith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Serenade by Judith Leyster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJudith_Leyster_Serenade.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/500px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/1280px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg/500px-Serenade_in_the_Ottoman_Empire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Serenade in the Ottoman empire, 1688","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A